Scenario The list is in two sections, what is owned and what is owed
Description A house has no heading of its own and sits straight under Assets;
Description a mortgage sits straight under Liabilities. The card is under
Description Liabilities with the mortgage, which is the whole point of the two
Description sections: a card is money owed.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                 | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking      | Bank       | false       |
| Assets:Savings       | Bank       | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage     | Investment | false       |
| Assets:House         | Asset      | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa     | CreditCard | false       |
| Liabilities:Mortgage | Liability  | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee | Account              | Amount     |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Assets:Checking      | 2455.00    |
| T2  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Assets:Savings       | 500.00     |
| T3  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Assets:Brokerage     | 9000.00    |
| T4  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Assets:House         | 200000.00  |
| T5  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Liabilities:Visa     | -89.99     |
| T6  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Liabilities:Mortgage | -150000.00 |
When account list shown
Then account list rows are : AccountListRow
| Section     | Group       | Account              | Name      | Indent | Balance   | IsHeading |
| Assets      | none        | none                 | none      | 0      | 211955.00 | true      |
| Assets      | Banking     | none                 | none      | 1      | 2955.00   | true      |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:Checking      | Checking  | 2      | 2455.00   | false     |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:Savings       | Savings   | 2      | 500.00    | false     |
| Assets      | Investments | none                 | none      | 1      | 9000.00   | true      |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:Brokerage     | Brokerage | 2      | 9000.00   | false     |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:House         | House     | 1      | 200000.00 | false     |
| Liabilities | none        | none                 | none      | 0      | 150089.99 | true      |
| Liabilities | CreditCards | none                 | none      | 1      | 89.99     | true      |
| Liabilities | none        | Liabilities:Visa     | Visa      | 2      | 89.99     | false     |
| Liabilities | none        | Liabilities:Mortgage | Mortgage  | 1      | 150000.00 | false     |
# The groups that have a heading come first, in the order they are declared,
# and the section's own accounts come after them. Every figure is the display
# balance, so the card and the mortgage read as what is owed and the two
# section totals are the two sides of a balance sheet: 211,955.00 owned,
# 150,089.99 owed, 61,865.01 net.

Scenario A group with no accounts is not shown
Description There is nothing under Investments, Assets or Liabilities in this
Description book, so those headings are left out rather than shown empty.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account list shown
Then account list groups shown are : GroupShown
| Group       |
| Banking     |
| CreditCards |

Attributes GroupShown
| Attribute | Type | Default |
| Group     | Text |         |

$WIP
Scenario A hidden account is left out until it is asked for
Description Hiding an account is how it is got out of the way without losing its
Description history, so the list follows that. The total of the group follows
Description the list, so hiding an account changes what the heading says.
