When payee rule asked for
Then rule offered is : PayeeRule Vertical
| Pattern   | SHELL OIL |
| MatchType | Contains  |
| Payee     | SHELL OIL |
| Category  | none      |
| Enabled   | true      |
# Uncategorized is not a category anybody chose, so it is not offered as one. A
# rule carrying it would put every future visit back in the bucket it is the
# program's job to empty.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# From a figure in a report to the transaction behind it
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description A report that shows its transactions should let one be opened. The
Description figure is the question; the register is where the answer is, and
Description where it can be corrected.
Details The register opened is the one of the real account the transaction
Details touches -- the bank or the card side. A category has no register to
Details browse: categories are reached through a report, which is where the
Details click started.
Details
Details The line is selected, and the window scrolls it into view. Twenty years
Details of history is tens of thousands of lines, so a selection nobody can see
Details is the same as no selection at all.

Attributes ReportLineSelect
Description Which line of the report was clicked, counting from one.
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Line      | Integer | 1       |

Define FebruaryOnChecking
Description The book the next three scenarios read. Two visits to a filling
Description station and one to a supermarket, so that one category figure has
Description more than one transaction behind it.
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Account            | Amount |
| T1  | 2026-02-01 | Shell         | Assets:Checking    | -40.00 |
| T1  | 2026-02-01 | Shell         | Expenses:Auto:Fuel | 40.00  |
| T2  | 2026-02-05 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking    | -60.00 |
| T2  | 2026-02-05 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries | 60.00  |
| T3  | 2026-02-10 | Shell         | Assets:Checking    | -30.00 |
| T3  | 2026-02-10 | Shell         | Expenses:Auto:Fuel | 30.00  |

$WIP
Scenario Clicking a transaction in the report opens its register at that line
Description The fifth line of the report is the second of the two visits to the
Description filling station. It is the third line of the checking register, and
Description that is where the click lands.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Auto      | Expense | true        |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
=FebruaryOnChecking
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category     |
| From     | 2026-02-01   |
| To       | 2026-02-28   |
| Interval | Whole        |
| Detail   | Transactions |
When report line clicked : ReportLineSelect Vertical
| Line | 5 |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing  | Account         | Active |
| 1    | Register | Assets:Checking | true   |
Then the register line selected is : RegisterSelect
| Line |
| 3    |
# The report reads: Expenses, Expenses:Auto, Expenses:Auto:Fuel, the 1 February
# visit, the 10 February visit, Expenses:Groceries, the supermarket. So line
# five is the 10 February visit, and the checking register in date order has it
# third. Assets:Checking is the register opened because it is the real account
# the transaction touches; Expenses:Auto:Fuel has no register to browse.

