Attributes IdShown
Description Whether the id of one transaction is shown, and whether the two
Description places that show it agree.
| Attribute | Type      | Default |
| Date      | Date      |         |
| Payee     | PayeeName |         |
| Blank     | Boolean   | false   |
| TheSame   | Boolean   | true    |

$WIP
Scenario The report and the register show the same transaction id
Description Shown in both places while the click-through is being checked: it
Description is how a line on one page is known to be the line on the other.
Description The id is a clock reading to the millisecond, so no table can write
Description it down -- what is checked is that it is there and that the two
Description agree. Expected to come off both pages once the navigation is
Description trusted; see the naming rule in Transactions for what it is.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Bank    | false       |
| Expenses:Auto      | Expense | true        |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
=FebruaryOnChecking
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category     |
| From     | 2026-02-01   |
| To       | 2026-02-28   |
| Interval | Whole        |
| Detail   | Transactions |
Then the transaction id shown is : IdShown
| Date       | Payee         | Blank | TheSame |
| 2026-02-01 | Shell         | false | true    |
| 2026-02-05 | Harris Teeter | false | true    |
| 2026-02-10 | Shell         | false | true    |
# Three transactions, three ids, and each one the same string in the report as
# in the register. Two transactions sharing an id would make the click-through
# land on the wrong line and is the thing this is really watching for.
